WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:02.580
(gentle orchestral music)

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.200
- [Narrator] These days,
synthetic dyes are everywhere.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.700
Ninety-nine percent of fabrics
are dyed with chemicals

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.750
we can barely even pronounce.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:14.130
But before there was
azophloxin, chrysoidine R,

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.530
and Xylene cyanol FF, there was saffron,

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.093
madder root, and tree bark.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.290
In Kyoto, Japan, Sachio
Yoshioka and his team

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.667
are creating dyes the
traditional way-with plants.

00:00:32.106 --> 00:00:33.802
(bouncy string music)

00:00:33.802 --> 00:00:36.719
(foreign language)

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:01.910
Chemical dyes are bad for the environment

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.110
and end up polluting the
Earth's water supply.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:07.890
Sachio and his team use
locally grown plants

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.370
to create their bright and colorful dyes.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.287
(foreign language)

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.040
The natural dyes are
used to create fabric,

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.030
which is made into
traditional Japanese costumes

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:46.996
but also everyday wares.

00:01:46.996 --> 00:01:49.996
(foreign language)

